      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The parent alloy has been assessed under cooling conditions spanning approximately 10^2 to 10^6 K/s.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::005::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding up to approximately 2 at.% B will suppress initiation of primary crystallization in Cr16Mn16Fe16Co16Ni16P20.",
      "field": "hypothesis; intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The B-modified alloy can be prepared by arc melting followed by rapid quenching or melt spinning.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B addition will increase retained amorphous fraction after moderate cooling at approximately 10^2–10^3 K/s.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B addition will increase retained amorphous fraction after rapid cooling at approximately 10^4–10^6 K/s.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B addition will improve resistance to devitrification during subsequent reheating.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B–metal complexes form in the supercooled liquid.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "B–metal complexes reduce atomic mobility and stabilize the amorphous network.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strong B-related chemical bonds raise the nucleation energy barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The raised nucleation barrier extends the supercooled-liquid region and delays or suppresses primary crystallization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the undoped alloy, the B-doped alloy will show a higher DSC crystallization-onset temperature.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effect will be most pronounced at cooling rates of at least approximately 10^2 K/s.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effect will remain significant during DSC reheating at approximately 10–20 K/min.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A prior amorphous-ribbon study conducted thermal analysis at 20 K/min and observed a glass transition followed by two crystallization exotherms.",
